From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:48:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 41/59] ntdll: Set up every game that comes with DLSS for DLSS
 on  Mullion.

A game MetalSharp launched on the Mullion backend that comes with NVIDIA's DLSS (nvngx_dlss.dll,
nvngx_dlssd.dll) or Streamline (sl.interposer.dll) anywhere in its folder (its steamapps/common/<game> folder,
the one above an Unreal Engine project's, else its program's) is shown an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4080 with driver
617.14 in Windows' device list, unless its winemac.conf section names another GPU. With an NVIDIA GPU there,
Mullion is told to show the same one (MULLION_CONFIG gains dxgi.customVendorId, customDeviceId and
customDeviceDesc) and its NVIDIA extension is on (MULLION_ENABLE_NVEXT=1, unless set). A Streamline game is
hidden Wine's exports as well (METALSHARP_HIDE_WINE_EXPORTS, which the loader reads): The Witcher 3 starts
Streamline only without wine_get_version. The search is kept in <program's folder>/.metalsharp/dlss while it is
newer than the program.
